# Orbit-RS Gaming Example: Real-Time Leaderboards
# Using Redis Sorted Sets (ZSET) for high-performance ranking

# 1. Update Scores (ZADD key score member)
# Simulate match results updating player ELO ratings
ZADD leaderboard:season_1 1500 "Slayer99"
ZADD leaderboard:season_1 1450 "HealerPro"
ZADD leaderboard:season_1 1600 "TankMaster"
ZADD leaderboard:season_1 1200 "Newbie01"
ZADD leaderboard:season_1 1550 "RogueOne"

# 2. Get Top 3 Players (ZREVRANGE key start stop WITHSCORES)
# High score is better
ZREVRANGE leaderboard:season_1 0 2 WITHSCORES

# 3. Get Player Rank (ZREVRANK key member)
# 0-based index, 0 is rank #1
ZREVRANK leaderboard:season_1 "Slayer99"

# 4. Get Players Around a User (Contextual Leaderboard)
# Useful for "You are ranked X, here are players near you"
# Assume Slayer99 is rank 2 (index 2). We want rank 1-3.
ZREVRANGE leaderboard:season_1 1 3 WITHSCORES

# 5. Atomic Score Increment (ZINCRBY)
# Player wins a match, gains 25 points
ZINCRBY leaderboard:season_1 25 "Slayer99"

# 6. Verify New Score
ZSCORE leaderboard:season_1 "Slayer99"
